      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The need for standardized and unified performance capacity assessment in orthopedic rehabilitation has led to the attempt to use an existing standardized procedure. Graduated disease features have been defined which are relevant for work and their effects on performance capacity been formulated as rules. In this way so-called disease-conditioned performance capacities are obtained which help to identify problems in carrying out various activities. These activities can be directly assessed using tests. Appropriate tests are listed in a table."},
